# Active Directory Home Lab

## Overview

This repository documents the design, deployment, administration, and troubleshooting of a Microsoft Active Directory environment built in Oracle VirtualBox.

The project simulates a small business network from the ground up, beginning with the deployment of a Windows Server Domain Controller and expanding into a complete enterprise-style environment.

Throughout this project, I will configure core Windows Server services including Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS), DNS, DHCP, Group Policy, file sharing, user and group management, and Windows client administration.

The objective is to strengthen my practical Windows Server administration skills while building a professional portfolio that demonstrates hands-on experience in enterprise IT environments.

---

# Project Objectives

- Deploy Windows Server as a Domain Controller
- Configure Active Directory Domain Services
- Configure DNS
- Configure DHCP
- Create Organizational Units
- Create and manage users
- Create and manage security groups
- Join Windows clients to the domain
- Configure Group Policy Objects (GPOs)
- Configure shared folders and NTFS permissions
- Implement mapped network drives
- Perform Active Directory administration
- Troubleshoot common Helpdesk scenarios
- Document all work using industry-standard documentation

